WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:05.040
Actor Cuba Gooding Jr. has had some&nbsp;
ups and downs in both his professional&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.040 --> 00:00:10.240
and personal life. As with many Oscar winners,&nbsp;
the road toward continued success is often&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:10.240 --> 00:00:15.920
paved with lots of twists and turns. Here's why&nbsp;
Hollywood won't cast Cuba Gooding Jr. anymore.

00:00:16.480 --> 00:00:21.280
To get the elephant out of the room: The most&nbsp;
obvious reason Cuba Gooding Jr. isn't being&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:21.280 --> 00:00:25.840
sought out for roles anymore is that numerous&nbsp;
women have accused him of sexual misconduct.

00:00:25.840 --> 00:00:30.000
It started in June of 2019, when&nbsp;
USA Today reported that Gooding was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:34.560
being investigated for allegedly groping a&nbsp;
woman while drunk at a bar in New York City.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:34.560 --> 00:00:40.240
Gooding was later arrested after turning himself&nbsp;
in to the NYPD, as USA Today later confirmed.

00:00:40.240 --> 00:00:43.200
He was eventually released&nbsp;
pending a further trial.

00:00:43.200 --> 00:00:47.120
In October of that same year, The New York&nbsp;
Times reported that Gooding was indicted on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:47.120 --> 00:00:51.440
a separate sexual abuse charge. Though details&nbsp;
about the new allegations weren't released,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:51.440 --> 00:00:55.280
they were serious enough that they&nbsp;
delayed the trial for the June incident.

00:00:55.280 --> 00:00:59.680
The same New York Times report also noted that&nbsp;
Gooding denied all allegations against him,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:59.680 --> 00:01:04.000
and that his lawyers had tried unsuccessfully&nbsp;
to get the original charges dismissed.

00:01:04.000 --> 00:01:07.200
Some believe the trouble began earlier than 2019.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:07.200 --> 00:01:11.040
Page Six reported that ever since Gooding's&nbsp;
divorce from his high school sweetheart,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:11.040 --> 00:01:17.440
Sara Kapfer, in 2014, the actor has spent his free&nbsp;
time clubbing, partying, and drinking heavily,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:17.440 --> 00:01:22.000
while displaying some of the questionable&nbsp;
behavior detailed in the assault allegations.

00:01:22.000 --> 00:01:24.000
"I was in a club the other night, broke my ankle."

00:01:25.120 --> 00:01:25.760
"What are you talking about?"

00:01:25.760 --> 00:01:27.008
"Well, I sprained it."

00:01:27.200 --> 00:01:30.320
Not long after the second woman&nbsp;
made charges against Gooding,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:30.320 --> 00:01:34.400
Page Six reported that three more women&nbsp;
had come forward to accuse the actor of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:34.400 --> 00:01:39.760
misconduct. The report stated that these&nbsp;
new allegations dated back as far as 2008,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:39.760 --> 00:01:45.280
and included instances of Gooding groping two of&nbsp;
the women in similar ways on separate occasions.

00:01:45.280 --> 00:01:50.720
By the end of 2019, NBC News reported that the&nbsp;
number of women accusing Gooding of misconduct&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:50.720 --> 00:01:54.880
had grown to 22, which included&nbsp;
an additional seven women coming&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:54.880 --> 00:01:58.960
forward with detailed stories that&nbsp;
involved instances of forced kissing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:58.960 --> 00:02:04.080
and Gooding giving graphic depictions of sexual&nbsp;
acts, among other inappropriate behaviors.

00:02:04.080 --> 00:02:08.560
The coming year proved to be even worse for&nbsp;
Gooding, as CNN reported the number of accusers&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:08.560 --> 00:02:13.920
had grown to a staggering 30 women by August&nbsp;
2020. Gooding also officially got charged with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:13.920 --> 00:02:19.920
three counts of forcible touching and three counts&nbsp;
of sexual abuse. He still denies all wrongdoing.

00:02:19.920 --> 00:02:23.440
As of the time of the CNN report,&nbsp;
Gooding's defense was working to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:23.440 --> 00:02:27.280
undermine the credibility of the accusers&nbsp;
by using their past statements against&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:27.280 --> 00:02:30.960
them and to question the procedural&nbsp;
propriety of the police investigation.

00:02:31.840 --> 00:02:35.920
In addition to the multiple criminal&nbsp;
accusations, two women have filed civil&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:35.920 --> 00:02:40.800
suits against Gooding. In August 2020, The&nbsp;
New York Times reported that a lawsuit was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:40.800 --> 00:02:46.720
filed against the actor by a woman accusing&nbsp;
him of sexually assaulting her twice in 2013.

00:02:46.720 --> 00:02:51.120
The lawsuit stated that the woman, referred&nbsp;
to as Jane Doe, met Gooding at a Greenwich&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:51.120 --> 00:02:55.200
Village restaurant, and the actor invited&nbsp;
her to have drinks with him at a hotel in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:55.200 --> 00:02:59.520
SoHo. Gooding eventually invited her to his&nbsp;
hotel room; when the woman tried to leave,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:59.520 --> 00:03:01.840
she said Gooding attacked and raped her.

00:03:01.840 --> 00:03:06.000
This follows a different lawsuit that&nbsp;
was filed earlier in 2019 by one of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:06.000 --> 00:03:09.920
the many women who accused Gooding&nbsp;
of groping. According to Page Six,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:09.920 --> 00:03:14.080
bartender Natasha Ashworth was working at&nbsp;
a nightclub when Gooding approached her.

00:03:14.080 --> 00:03:17.440
After denying his advances,&nbsp;
Gooding then proceeded to grope her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:17.440 --> 00:03:21.040
several times. Unlike the 2020&nbsp;
suit, the same Page Six report&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:21.040 --> 00:03:25.920
noted the events that transpired within&nbsp;
the 2019 lawsuit happened a year prior.

00:03:25.920 --> 00:03:31.680
In June 2021, Complex reported that Ashworth&nbsp;
won her lawsuit in a default judgment—basically&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:31.680 --> 00:03:35.280
meaning that Gooding simply failed&nbsp;
to respond to the lawsuit at all.

00:03:36.160 --> 00:03:39.680
Even before all the sexual misconduct&nbsp;
allegations against him were revealed,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:39.680 --> 00:03:45.840
Cuba Gooding Jr.'s career&nbsp;
wasn't what it used to be.

00:03:45.840 --> 00:03:49.360
"Show. Me. The. Money!"

00:03:49.360 --> 00:03:51.200
After the success of Jerry Maguire,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:51.200 --> 00:03:56.080
Gooding suffered the same career slump that has&nbsp;
plagued many actors after they win an Oscar.

00:03:56.080 --> 00:03:59.360
Despite starring in films like the&nbsp;
well-received As Good As It Gets and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:59.360 --> 00:04:04.320
the box office hit Pearl Harbor, Gooding's&nbsp;
post-Oscar resume is plagued by a series&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:04.320 --> 00:04:08.880
of terrible comedies that have landed him&nbsp;
several Golden Raspberry Award nominations.

00:04:08.880 --> 00:04:12.640
Some of his more questionable career&nbsp;
decisions included the Eddie Murphy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:12.640 --> 00:04:17.280
misfire Norbit, the poorly reviewed and&nbsp;
little-seen Disney comedy Snow Dogs,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:17.280 --> 00:04:20.400
and the much-reviled family sequel Daddy Day Camp.

00:04:20.400 --> 00:04:25.120
Even with films like the Ridley Scott crime drama&nbsp;
American Gangster in between these mistakes,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:25.120 --> 00:04:30.400
it was clear that the days of critically acclaimed&nbsp;
films like Jerry Maguire were long past Gooding.

00:04:30.400 --> 00:04:35.040
Gooding has even acknowledged in an interview with&nbsp;
Page Six that he made several bad decisions for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:35.040 --> 00:04:40.400
his career, including revealing he turned down&nbsp;
roles in several acclaimed films like Amistad,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:40.400 --> 00:04:43.520
Ray, The Last King of Scotland, and Hotel Rwanda,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:43.520 --> 00:04:46.960
all of which went on to be&nbsp;
nominated for three Academy Awards.

00:04:46.960 --> 00:04:49.920
When asked why he made so&nbsp;
many poor career choices,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:49.920 --> 00:04:53.040
Gooding denied that he was&nbsp;
motivated by money. He said:

00:04:53.040 --> 00:04:57.280
"For me, it was always about protecting the&nbsp;
sanctity of that golden statue. Because I&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:57.280 --> 00:05:00.480
felt I needed to show people that&nbsp;
I can do more, I can do better."

00:05:01.200 --> 00:05:05.280
After several critical and commercial&nbsp;
failures, Gooding faded from the limelight,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:05.280 --> 00:05:09.760
but still managed to get work in the form of&nbsp;
several direct-to-DVD films. In fact, between&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:09.760 --> 00:05:15.760
the years of 2006 and 2013, Gooding appeared&nbsp;
in almost nothing but direct-to-DVD pictures.

00:05:15.760 --> 00:05:17.760
Like many movies that skip the theater,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:17.760 --> 00:05:22.960
these films mostly consisted of forgettable&nbsp;
action flicks and lackluster family offerings,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:22.960 --> 00:05:27.920
from hardboiled crime films like Wrong Turn&nbsp;
at Tahoe, which also starred a far-fallen&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:27.920 --> 00:05:34.960
Harvey Keitel, to animated numbers like 2007's&nbsp;
The Land Before Time XIII: The Wisdom of Friends.

00:05:34.960 --> 00:05:38.800
After this series of debacles, Gooding&nbsp;
made the jump back to feature films like&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:38.800 --> 00:05:44.480
the Tuskegee Airmen war film Red Tails and the&nbsp;
Robert Rodriguez-directed flick Machete Kills,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:44.480 --> 00:05:50.160
as well as supporting roles in Oscar-nominated&nbsp;
pictures such as Selma in 2014 and Lee Daniels'&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:50.160 --> 00:05:55.040
star-studded period piece The Butler&nbsp;
(2013). It wasn't exactly a comeback,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:55.040 --> 00:05:58.000
but it seemed like a promising&nbsp;
reprieve from all the dreck.

00:05:58.000 --> 00:06:02.080
Gooding also made the jump back to television,&nbsp;
with guest appearances in shows like the Fox&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:02.080 --> 00:06:07.920
hip-hop drama Empire and the short-lived ABC drama&nbsp;
Forever, as well as TV movies like Gifted Hands,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:07.920 --> 00:06:11.760
where he played neurosurgeon and&nbsp;
presidential candidate Ben Carson.

00:06:11.760 --> 00:06:16.080
"And then I read this screenplay and saw&nbsp;
that he was raised by a single mother&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:16.080 --> 00:06:20.400
who instilled his faith in God.&nbsp;
And my mom was the exact same way."

00:06:20.400 --> 00:06:24.080
While the latter film landed Gooding&nbsp;
a Screen Actors Guild nomination for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:24.080 --> 00:06:29.280
Outstanding Performance by a Male Actor in a&nbsp;
Miniseries-slash-TV Movie, none of these film&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:29.280 --> 00:06:34.160
or television roles lit the entertainment world&nbsp;
on fire the same way Gooding's past projects did.

00:06:34.880 --> 00:06:39.200
Many actors retreat from the spotlight in&nbsp;
order to focus on working behind the camera,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:39.200 --> 00:06:43.600
something that Gooding tried his hand&nbsp;
at in 2018. Gooding's directorial debut&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:43.600 --> 00:06:47.920
came in the form of Bayou Caviar, an&nbsp;
action film that he also co-wrote.

00:06:47.920 --> 00:06:52.000
In this film, Gooding starred as Rodney&nbsp;
Jones, a retired boxer who gets mixed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:52.000 --> 00:06:56.480
up with Russian mobsters and is tasked with&nbsp;
gathering information for a blackmail scheme&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:56.480 --> 00:07:01.440
against a real estate mogul. The film also&nbsp;
starred Famke Janssen as a photographer who&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:01.440 --> 00:07:06.000
aids Jones on his quest and the legendary&nbsp;
Richard Dreyfuss as the main mobster.

00:07:06.000 --> 00:07:10.480
Despite a strong supporting cast, the&nbsp;
film was not well received by critics.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:10.480 --> 00:07:13.920
And considering it came out a year&nbsp;
before the misconduct allegations did,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:13.920 --> 00:07:17.440
it's not surprising that he hasn't&nbsp;
stepped back into the director's chair.

00:07:18.640 --> 00:07:22.720
Megaproducer Ryan Murphy cast Gooding in&nbsp;
the first season of American Crime Story,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:22.720 --> 00:07:27.200
which covered the infamous O.J. Simpson&nbsp;
trial and accompanying media circus.

00:07:27.200 --> 00:07:31.600
Gooding was cast as Simpson, the disgraced&nbsp;
former athlete and actor at the center of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:31.600 --> 00:07:36.160
the show. Playing Simpson was similar to the&nbsp;
role that made Gooding famous. The actor said:

00:07:36.160 --> 00:07:39.920
"I say this is my second stab at&nbsp;
Rod Tidwell from Jerry Maguire,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:39.920 --> 00:07:43.120
because both of these personalities&nbsp;
are born from this thing that happens&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:43.120 --> 00:07:47.120
with athletes [...] One had a positive&nbsp;
outcome and this one had a negative [one]."

00:07:47.120 --> 00:07:51.520
Perhaps that's why both Gooding's performance&nbsp;
and the series itself were critically acclaimed;&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:51.520 --> 00:07:54.720
Gooding even scored an Emmy&nbsp;
nomination for his performance.

00:07:54.720 --> 00:07:57.840
"O.J., did you do it?"

00:08:00.160 --> 00:08:00.660
"No."

00:08:01.280 --> 00:08:05.280
Gooding followed up this well-received&nbsp;
performance with another Ryan Murphy project,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:05.280 --> 00:08:09.040
as a main cast member of the sixth&nbsp;
season of American Horror Story,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:09.040 --> 00:08:12.880
subtitled Roanoke. Gooding starred&nbsp;
alongside Sarah Paulson as a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:12.880 --> 00:08:16.960
married couple terrorized by a group of&nbsp;
killers after moving to North Carolina.

00:08:16.960 --> 00:08:20.000
Though not as critically&nbsp;
acclaimed as American Crime Story,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:20.000 --> 00:08:22.320
Roanoke still received positive reviews.

00:08:22.320 --> 00:08:26.080
Both Ryan Murphy projects brought Gooding&nbsp;
back into the spotlight for a short time,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:26.080 --> 00:08:31.520
but they also led to yet another controversial&nbsp;
incident. During a 2017 event promoting his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:31.520 --> 00:08:36.080
American Horror Story season, Gooding was caught&nbsp;
lifting up Sarah Paulson's skirt when she got up&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:36.080 --> 00:08:41.520
to greet actress Kathy Bates at the event. Despite&nbsp;
backlash for his actions, Gooding shrugged it off.

00:08:41.520 --> 00:08:43.200
"I see Sarah Paulson as my sister."

00:08:43.760 --> 00:08:47.600
After both his runs on American&nbsp;
Horror Story and American Crime Story,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:47.600 --> 00:08:52.000
it seemed like Gooding would be hot on the&nbsp;
screen market once again. Instead, he made&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:52.000 --> 00:08:57.200
a slightly unexpected move with a brief stint&nbsp;
on stage. He'd already appeared on Broadway for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:57.200 --> 00:09:02.320
2013's well-received play The Trip to Bountiful,&nbsp;
but had yet to appear in a musical production.

00:09:02.320 --> 00:09:06.880
In 2018, he was cast in the London&nbsp;
West End theater revival of Chicago,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:06.880 --> 00:09:12.160
playing the role of sleazy defense lawyer&nbsp;
Billy Flynn. A turn on Broadway can showcase&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:12.160 --> 00:09:17.120
an actor's range while also earning them a good&nbsp;
living, but Gooding said he just wanted to:

00:09:17.120 --> 00:09:20.720
"See if I could pull off a&nbsp;
musical. That was the main reason."

00:09:20.720 --> 00:09:25.280
Reviews for Gooding's performance, and for the&nbsp;
show overall, were mixed. While certain outlets&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:25.280 --> 00:09:28.960
like The Guardian gave relatively positive&nbsp;
remarks to both Gooding's performance and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:28.960 --> 00:09:33.360
the show as a whole, other reviewers like&nbsp;
London Theatre were much more critical of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:33.360 --> 00:09:37.840
the lackluster production value and the&nbsp;
uninspired take on the long-running show.

00:09:37.840 --> 00:09:41.360
"I've played ice hockey 20 years.&nbsp;
I've boxed almost professionally.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:41.920 --> 00:09:45.760
And nothing prepared me for singing&nbsp;
and dancing eight shows a week."

00:09:45.760 --> 00:09:48.560
Gooding's run as Billy Flynn&nbsp;
was short-lived. He concluded&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:48.560 --> 00:09:52.400
his run on September 1 of that year&nbsp;
before being replaced by Brian Kemp,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:52.400 --> 00:09:57.360
though he returned to the role twice&nbsp;
for brief runs in both 2018 and 2019.

00:09:58.160 --> 00:10:03.120
The current-day problems that have surrounded&nbsp;
Gooding have stalled his career almost completely.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:03.120 --> 00:10:08.960
As of 2021, the only notable film that Gooding&nbsp;
starred in was the 2020 romantic drama film&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:08.960 --> 00:10:14.560
Life in a Year, which starred Jaden Smith and&nbsp;
Cara Delevingne as teenage lovers who decide to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:14.560 --> 00:10:19.120
live their lives to the fullest when Delevingne's&nbsp;
character reveals that she has terminal cancer.

00:10:19.120 --> 00:10:24.720
The film held promise; it also starred Nia&nbsp;
Long and RZA, and was executive produced by&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:24.720 --> 00:10:29.120
Jaden's parents, Will and Jada Pinkett Smith.&nbsp;
But with negative reviews, limited streaming&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:29.120 --> 00:10:34.400
distribution, and another star accused of sexual&nbsp;
misconduct, the movie was quickly forgotten.

00:10:34.400 --> 00:10:39.360
Despite various court appearances and no other&nbsp;
film or television projects on the horizon,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:39.360 --> 00:10:43.520
the Daily Mail has reported the actor was&nbsp;
recently seen partying in Los Angeles,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:43.520 --> 00:10:45.880
bar hopping and mingling with other patrons.

00:10:46.880 --> 00:10:51.280
With another lawsuit pending and many other&nbsp;
allegations still under investigation,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:51.280 --> 00:10:55.440
it's safe to say that Gooding won't be&nbsp;
making another comeback anytime soon. With&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:55.440 --> 00:11:00.400
sexual misconduct allegations being taken more&nbsp;
seriously after the rise of the MeToo movement,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:00.400 --> 00:11:05.520
most Hollywood studios wouldn't dare employ&nbsp;
someone as controversial as Cuba Gooding Jr.,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:05.520 --> 00:11:08.560
especially with a list of accusers as long as his.

00:11:08.560 --> 00:11:13.040
Whether or not Gooding tries to mount a&nbsp;
comeback — either by more Direct-To-DVD films,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:13.040 --> 00:11:17.120
another directing gig, or some other form&nbsp;
of entertainment — remains to be seen.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:17.120 --> 00:11:21.520
But numerous pending court appearances&nbsp;
will most likely keep him busy for a while.

00:11:22.160 --> 00:11:25.280
If you or anyone you know has&nbsp;
been a victim of sexual assault,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:25.280 --> 00:11:29.360
help is available. Visit the Rape,&nbsp;
Abuse &amp; Incest National Network&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:29.360 --> 00:11:37.680
website or contact RAINN's National&nbsp;
Helpline at 1-800-656-HOPE (4673).

